    "Description": "rhc is a client tool and daemon that connects the system to Red Hat hosted services enabling system and subscription management.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* mime: golang: Golang MIME: Denial of Service via maliciously-crafted MIME header (CVE-2026-42504)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* rhc package uninstall/remove leaves /etc/rhc and /etc/rhc/workers directories on the hosts. (JIRA:RHEL-152311)\n\n* [rhc]Installation in container raises warnings (JIRA:RHEL-138412)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n\nAdditional Changes:\n\nFor detailed information on changes in this release, see the Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9 Release Notes linked from the References section.",
